{"term":{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SO_0000336","compactId":"SO_0000336","id":"SO:0000336","label":"pseudogene","definition":{"text":"A sequence that closely resembles a known functional gene, at another locus within a genome, that is non-functional as a consequence of (usually several) mutations that prevent either its transcription or translation (or both). In general, pseudogenes result from either reverse transcription of a transcript of their \"normal\" paralog (SO:0000043) (in which case the pseudogene typically lacks introns and includes a poly(A) tail) or from recombination (SO:0000044) (in which case the pseudogene is typically a tandem duplication of its \"normal\" paralog).","xrefs":["http://www.ucl.ac.uk/~ucbhjow/b241/glossary.html"]},"comments":[],"synonyms":[{"scope":"exact","value":"INSDC_qualifier:pseudo"},{"scope":"exact","value":"INSDC_qualifier:unknown"},{"scope":"broad","value":"INSDC_feature:gene"}],"xrefs":["http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pseudogene"],"subsets":["Alliance_of_Genome_Resources","SOFA"],"altIds":[],"namespace":"sequence","isObsolete":false,"replacedBy":[],"canonicalUrl":"/browser/current_release/term/SO:0000336/","history":{"firstSeen":{"hash":"92e3cae9f3d39e5979110bad332c5fadf7a4b3ab","shortHash":"92e3cae","date":"2016-12-05","subject":"Add renamed SO files","issueRefs":[]},"mostRecent":{"hash":"cb6662b4faae5207ad48274fe2a265702b583494","shortHash":"cb6662b","date":"2020-03-27","subject":"Added Alliance_of_Genome_Resources subset","issueRefs":[]},"entries":[{"hash":"cb6662b4faae5207ad48274fe2a265702b583494","shortHash":"cb6662b","date":"2020-03-27","subject":"Added Alliance_of_Genome_Resources subset","issueRefs":[]},{"hash":"5fe48bd4b720f8b140cb0f77461798c55532c097","shortHash":"5fe48bd","date":"2018-01-26","subject":"Add INSDC mappings","issueRefs":[]},{"hash":"92e3cae9f3d39e5979110bad332c5fadf7a4b3ab","shortHash":"92e3cae","date":"2016-12-05","subject":"Add renamed SO files","issueRefs":[]}],"semanticEvents":[{"type":